{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"3750a08f7e1211efa623726b09d239bd8b88e94f868a0adc370a3ff1a5fc77d0","slug":"metadata.publication","location":"/metadata/publication.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Metadata publication","content_includes_title":false,"authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"World Fair CDIF working group","given":"World Fair CDIF","non_dropping_particle":"working","family":"group"},"name":"World Fair CDIF working group","id":"contributors-myst-generated-uid-0"}],"github":"https://github.com/Cross-Domain-Interoperability-Framework/cdifbook","numbering":{"title":{"offset":2}},"source_url":"https://github.com/Cross-Domain-Interoperability-Framework/cdifbook/blob/main/metadata/publication.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/Cross-Domain-Interoperability-Framework/cdifbook/edit/main/metadata/publication.md","thumbnail":"/cdifbook/preview-2026-05/build/fig-flowchart-25e2c340f4fac3812801cd4159b5f370.jpg","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"publication.md","url":"/cdifbook/preview-2026-05/build/publication-3fa14f70954a736e75ac93afb7ee80ef.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This section describes workflows recommended for a metadata publisher to make their metadata accessible to Web crawlers for search engines to index their resources. The figure below is a flow chart showing the decision tree to determine how to expose metadata. Numbers in the following discussion refer to numbered boxes in the diagram.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"ea7Kfzg373"}],"key":"UGJ8d0gs37"},{"type":"image","url":"/cdifbook/preview-2026-05/build/fig-flowchart-25e2c340f4fac3812801cd4159b5f370.jpg","alt":"metadatapubworkflow","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"LBgo1FyjJL","urlSource":"./figures/fig-flowchart.jpg"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Figure. Decision graph to determine where metadata is located, from the resource publisher’s perspective. Steps are numbers and referenced in text.","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"JkcPS2I6Cu"}],"key":"g9jBfg13jk"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option 1. Embedded in HTML","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"Fgo6rCI47J"}],"identifier":"option-1-embedded-in-html","label":"Option 1. Embedded in HTML","html_id":"option-1-embedded-in-html","implicit":true,"key":"LJFOZqnBvi"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":10,"column":1},"end":{"line":10,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Starting at the top (1) in the above figure, if there are HTML landing pages that describe the resources of interest, and the metadata publisher has the necessary authority to update the content of these pages, then CDIF metadata serialised as JSON-LD (see Appendix 1) should be embedded in an HTML <script> element in the <head> section of each landing page (3). The script should have the following type and profile attributes:","position":{"start":{"line":10,"column":1},"end":{"line":10,"column":1}},"key":"O4J79jxDS3"}],"key":"YXLf0VVwtO"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"type=\"application/ld+json\" profile=\"CDIF1.0\"","key":"dLvfpAAgZi"}],"key":"mXR90RxWfH"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option 2. Individual metadata file URLs","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"key":"Nr3uOROBO7"}],"identifier":"option-2-individual-metadata-file-urls","label":"Option 2. Individual metadata file URLs","html_id":"option-2-individual-metadata-file-urls","implicit":true,"key":"M5cS3CcLVo"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the resources of interest do not have individual landing pages, or the metadata publisher does not have authority to update the content of landing pages, the metadata should be placed in a Web-accessible location (step 4 in the figure above). There are two common approaches:","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"key":"oaTimZ7DKi"}],"key":"ohLveJ7YBr"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each metadata record is accessed in a separate, static file with its own URL. The CDIF metadata is serialised as JSON-LD (see ","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"key":"lOQKGnyq8l"},{"type":"link","url":"/metadata/schemaorgimplementationpatterns","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Schema.org implementation","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"key":"YGiHDofnha"}],"urlSource":"./schemaOrgImplementationpatterns.md","dataUrl":"/metadata.schemaorgimplementationpatterns.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"gd1Dw8El6d"},{"type":"text","value":" ). MIME type for the metadata file, returned as the Content-Type parameter in the HTTP response header, is:","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"key":"TnmmcVtItV"}],"key":"XqMOv4JkBv"}],"key":"DNjH8vHIcc"}],"key":"haNkczy2F9"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"type=\"application/ld+json\" profile=\"CDIF1.0\"","key":"J5l7sIjKOq"}],"ke